  <ym-title|Final integration review of Chapters6,7,9><label|final-integration-review-of-chapters679>

  Reviewed the current corrected component allocation, the revised
  classical/weighted estimates, and the one-step theorem's supplier contract.
  Audit-only pass; no chapter edits.

  <section|Resolved local concerns><label|resolved-local-concerns>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Chapter6 global allocation is a genuine partition of unity and
    imposes the weak tests globally on every nonzero sector. Its300B
    restrictions are consequently justified.

    <item>Disjoint500B owner halos,200B action rows,304B Haar/protection
    rows,10B active clearance and B/50 stencil radius are now distinguished
    and compatible. Single-orientation extracted squares exclude the
    probability weight; one final orientation average matches the globally
    weighted precision exactly.

    <item>The actual harvested-energy bound now subtracts the selected affine
    annular squares before claiming pointwise component suppression. The mean
    identity p=Tw and the positive mean-square sign check out. See the
    detailed primitive review for the algebra and source match.

    <item>Chapter7's revised classical stationary-jet proof applies the
    completed weighted inverse to gauge-annihilating cubic covectors, and its
    fixed-budget argument compares Wilson vertices using the same actual
    inverse/tangents. These address the previously identified pre-L gap. The
    weighted and radial checks are recorded in the Chapter7 review.

    <item>Chapter9's retained integral now explicitly includes the fine
    small-field indicator and correctly uses the forest tangent only through
    its curl agreement with W_a. Scalar normalization and the direct
    retained-cutoff proof were independently checked earlier.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Concrete remaining integration corrections sent to
  root><label|concrete-remaining-integration-corrections-sent-to-root>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><strong|Actual period restriction.> The one-step theorem currently
    asks for minimum auxiliary periods but does not explicitly restrict the
    original coarse torus. Chapter6 requires side n\<geqslant\>100(B+1);
    five-period localization also uses embedded original reflection/read
    cubes. Scott's localization proof uses <verbatim|2(w+4)\<less\>2
    barw\<less\>n>. State a sufficiently strong actual-side premise, e.g.
    n\<gtr\>2barw for the selected localization construction, or a declared
    stage minimum covering every required read. Uniformity then means uniform
    over periods satisfying this restriction, not all periods
    indiscriminately.

    <item><strong|Inherited ratio choice.> The preparatory paragraph says
    choose L with V_j/L fitting a fraction of H_pre, although H_pre is
    proportional to the coupling-dependent epsilon_m^reg. The proved estimate
    is <verbatim|(V_j/L) epsilon_(m+1)^reg>. Compare this with H_pre using a
    uniform bound for epsilon_(m+1)^reg / epsilon_m^reg. The ratio is bounded
    for the adjacent reference values, so the intended fixed-L choice is
    available; the current abbreviated statement omits its necessary factor.

    <item><strong|Common product supplier.> The paragraph after
    <verbatim|ch09:joint-input> still cites <verbatim|ch06:common-majorant>
    with summed quadratic-score hypotheses. Chapter6's concrete completed
    route instead uses bounded pointwise jets and
    <verbatim|ch06:actual-jet-integral>, together with the actual
    component/primitive construction and simultaneous tail events. Cite that
    actual route, or explicitly verify the aggregate quadratic-score
    assumptions before using the alternative theorem. This is a supplier
    mismatch in the exposition, not a reason to multiply marginal integral
    bounds.
  </enumerate>

  Apart from these specified corrections, this pass found no further wrong
  scalar, orientation factor, or retained-cutoff exponent in the reviewed
  interfaces. It does not certify the unexamined trajectory, tuning,
  cutoff-stability or continuum chapters.

  <section|Final correction verification><label|final-correction-verification>

  All three integration corrections above are resolved in the current
  Chapter9: the theorem now restricts the actual coarse period to cover the
  localization reads; the inherited comparison includes epsilon_(m+1) and its
  bounded adjacent ratio; and the joint product paragraph invokes the actual
  bounded-jet integral supplier. These items are no longer outstanding.
</body>

